   <dc:title>Systematic review and meta-analysis of the efficacy and safety of intermittent fasting in the metabolic syndrome in adults.</dc:title>
   <dc:creator>Figueroa Arango, Luis Alberto</dc:creator>
   <dc:contributor>García Morales, Olga Milena</dc:contributor>
   <dc:contributor>León, Henry</dc:contributor>
   <dc:contributor>de la Pava, Camilo</dc:contributor>
   <dc:contributor>Montoya Vargada, Francisco Javier</dc:contributor>
   <dc:subject>Metabolic syndrome</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Body mass index</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Body weight</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Hypertension</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Blood pressure</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Cholesterol</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Triglycerides</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Weight loss</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Obesity</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Metabolism</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Blood glucose</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Fasting</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Intermittent fasting</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Restricted feeding</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Time-restricted feeding</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Time-restricted eating</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Diet</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Ab libitum</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Normal diet</dc:subject>
   <dc:subject>Medicina</dc:subject>
   <dc:description>The study demonstrates that TRF can be an effective dietary strategy for improving metabolic health in overweight and obese adults with metabolic problems associated with metabolic syndrome, especially because it can be an additional strategy to the non-pharmacological measures for treating metabolic syndrome.</dc:description>
   <dc:description>The effects of intermittent fasting, specifically time-restricted feeding (TRF), on the metabolic syndrome were investigated in this meta-analysis. TRF can be considered as an additional strategy in the multidimensional intervention of metabolic syndrome since it has the potential to impact all the risk variables associated with the metabolic syndrome. The primary objective of this study is to look at the metabolic effects of intermittent fasting in adults with metabolic disorders associated with the metabolic syndrome. Secondary objectives include detecting changes in serologic fasting blood glucose, HDL cholesterol, and triglyceride levels; changes in blood pressure and anthropometric parameters such as weight, BMI, and WC; and examining the safety of TRF.</dc:description>
